# Quran Data Model

- `api/data.json` is the canonical schedule source for people, sections, parts, and rotation.
- Preserve the model unless explicitly asked to change it: 3 people, 3 sections, 7 days per week, 6 reading days, day 7 catch-up.
- Keep every `sections[].parts[]` aligned with `config.daysPerWeek`; reading days need numeric `verseStart`, `verseEnd`, and `page`.
- Keep `rotationPattern` rows the same length as `config.people`; values are 0-based indexes into `sections`.
- Changing person names affects `api/data.json`, HTML buttons, `assets/js/person.js`, CSS class maps, and persisted progress keys.
- Validate Quran ranges against `.cursor/docs/overview/SCHEDULE_REFERENCE.md` and `.cursor/docs/new-system-requests/CANONICAL_18_PARTS.md` before editing verse boundaries.
